# Analysis from the v1.0 release on a CPU machine. The raw logs are in logs/cpu_rerun/;
# this file points to the lines that matter.

Machine (cpu_rerun/check.txt): AMD EPYC 7V12 64-Core Processor, 128 threads, 503 GB RAM.
Code: commit 24ba290 (first line of cpu_rerun/check.txt, second of cpu_rerun/cpu_job.log).
Data: NO_IMAGES=1 scripts/setup.sh ("setup done: 2.9G"), detections.tar from the release with its
sha256 checked ("detections.tar: OK"), plus the release's yolo_yolo11n.pt_single__coco_val files.

Sections run one after another by scripts/run_analysis.sh (cpu_rerun/cpu_job.log):
[14:59:28] gate  [15:26:12] reproduction  [15:26:13] main  [15:54:29] audit  [16:21:36] stability
The run reached the fusion section at 16:50:27, after stability had finished, and was stopped there.

The remaining sections ran as separate scripts/analyze.py jobs: subgroups, finetune, errors,
prompts, contrasts and robustness in parallel from 16:42:43 (cpu_rerun/par_job.log and par_*.log),
fusion in a job of its own (cpu_rerun/fus_job.log, par_fusion.log). Each par_<section>.log holds the
"wrote results/<section>.json" line; par_job.log then shows figures.py.

COCO check printed by the gate section (measured AP, then the published AP in the code at 24ba290):
see cpu_rerun/cpu_job.log. LLMDet-T printed "55.5 None" because that code had no published value; the
LLMDet paper reports 55.6 (Table 4, trained with COCO images), which scripts/analyze.py and
results/gate.json carry.

Byte-for-byte comparison with the results computed on the GPU machine (cpu_rerun/check.txt):
identical: main.json, reproduction.json, audit.json, stability.json, fusion.json,
           finetune.json, prompts.json, contrasts.json.
gate.json, errors.json, subgroups.json and robustness.json come from this run's analysis code.

The unified_nms entries of results/robustness.json come from a separate `scripts/analyze.py unified_nms`
run from the same release (cpu_rerun/unified_nms_job.log).
